index 0000000..74d11f7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/01_specs/n28-execution-contract-v1.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# N28 closed execution contract (CPU preparation)
+
+No authority or executable release is produced by this implementation. The root alone reviews source, adopts the finite budget, performs the one new native proof, and releases the fresh screen. All templates remain disabled. An accepted CPU test is not an assigned-CUDA proof or task result.
+
+The only scientific delta from accepted N27 is the already accepted parent placement: initial four updates remain; ten selected-parent mutations precede original renoise; no rollout model-output updates. Model/noise/score schedule, quality, QD descriptor/selection, decoder/controller, Codex managed login, low/180s and no-Poe policy remain. RBF cost is **14 versus 19 calls per full guided chunk**, not equal total computation. Native model/score counts remain 21 batches and 176/11 canonical evaluations/batches.
+
+The new `_eds_renoise_reference` entry contains one passive observer call. Its numerical body, parameters and ordering are unchanged; the entire function is no longer byte-identical. Default pending state is empty. CPU tests compare original e21 methods and new default path, including that entry, and instrumentation on/off.
+
+The tensor resource tests `boundary_observer_binding_verified`: it calls the observer directly without renoise/noise/model execution. This is **not** actual renoise entry evidence. Live first-guided traces emitted at the real method entry separately bind the assigned prefix, exact Tensor object and timestep. Allocation sequence/source bytes -> parent witness/origins -> entry prefix are independently checked in the same metered worker. Initial witness retains original same-forward semantics; parent witness is explicitly current-chunk selected offspring. Assigned before/after and unconstrained proposal are separate. Transfer through subsequent RDT remains Unknown.
+
+## Source and historical bridge
+
+`qd_ed_n28_bridge` binds the 359-entry accepted e21 source record and four explicitly named historical JSONs: accepted N27 continuation terminal review, original 16-row N27 plan, accepted continuation source bridge and accepted original N27 native proof. It follows no nested historical attempt/runtime/tensor references and does not recursively execute old controllers. The accepted root closure is trusted for historical evidence/settlement. The original invalid attempt ID is preserved as a string, not a validity boolean.
+
+Whole-file reverse hunks bind four allowed old files: config.yaml, RDT steering policy, final runner and metered worker. All other old file hashes must match. New parent helper/profile, native reference/audit, scripts, tests and protocols enter the final manifest. Root must generate the bridge from the final committed source, then verify current frozen runtime/model/input bytes with the normal runner. Original N27 proof is referenced, not rerun or relabeled.
+
+Runtime inputs remain inside the frozen global artifact root. Only an N28 plan can place attempt output in the exact symlink `N28/artifacts` resolving to `<global>/variants/n28_parent_before_renoise`. The global runtime manifest/files/LIBERO config/task cache stay bound to the original root. Other queues keep their original artifact-root equality. Controller status, plan, proof and small reports live below N28; large attempt data uses its unified artifacts entry.
+
+## Schemas and activation order (root only)
+
+Every ref is `{path: absolute_path, sha256: exact_bytes_hash}`. Source is the existing `{commit, files:[{path,sha256}], sha256: canonical_files_hash}`. Existing runtime bytes are reused, not regenerated. All output JSON creation is exclusive; no overwrite/resume is authorized. Run commands from the adopted owning worktree with its `scripts` directory available to legacy CLI imports.
+
+1. Independently review final commit/diff, source manifest, reverse bytes, CPU evidence and all four actual runtime commands. Under idle private resource/state locks adopt `budget-adoption-v1/authority.json` schema `n28-finite-budget-authority-v1`; exact fields are `caps, protocol, predecessor, limits, local_gpu_hours, amendment, recorded_at, authority_interpretation, validation_authorized:false, formal_authorized:false`. Caps: 538 / 100h, baseline66/development232/validation180/formal40/recovery20; protected32/12h. Set state `n28_budget_authority` ref and exact budget fields. No component silently changes these values.
+2. From owning source construct the full source record and `qd_ed_n28_bridge.build(source, runtime_ref, root)`; write `source-equivalence-bridge-v1.json`. This is a CPU source bridge, not a native proof. Root current runtime/UUID/provider/login checks remain necessary.
+3. Write `arithmetic-preflight-source-review-v1.json` exactly as `backend.source_review` specifies: source/runtime/bridge, both protocols, accepted predecessor, finite budget and limits. Write/adopt `arithmetic-preflight-adoption-v1/authority.json` with schema `n28-arithmetic-resource-authority-v1`, source/runtime/source_review/budget_reuse/limits/current boot ID, automatic_retry:false and all phase authorizations false. State key `n28_arithmetic_authority`. Write the exact `arithmetic-preflight-release-v1.json` envelope. `python scripts/qd_ed_n28_backend.py --run` then permits at most one 80s + 40s resource process (24 fixed cases, no episode/model/API/sim). Health ledger retains reservation, dispatch and completed/aborted cost. It counts toward cumulative100h/local8.25h, using recovery GPU-hour category but **zero recovery episode slots**. Any failure consumes this scope and blocks Dev.
+4. Only after accepted strict native proof and settled process/health journal, write `final-source-runtime-review-v1.json` exactly as `contract.final_review` specifies. Write/adopt `adoption-v1/authority.json` schema `n28-screen-authority-v1` with exact source/runtime/protocol/final_review/budget_reuse/predecessor/limits/local_gpu_hours8.25 and descriptive time/interpretation; protected flags false. State key `n28_dev_authority`. No circular report hash is compiled into source.
+5. `python scripts/qd_ed_n28_prepare.py --output <N28>/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json --freeze`. Four arms C0/Q0/N27/N28, tasks0..3, original seeds/init mapping, task-major16. All primary capacity must fit; initial unprotected full local8.25h + protected reserves must fit100h. Each episode additionally needs the complete1840s local/cumulative coverage. No retry/substitution.
+6. Root verifies the exact16 commands through actual Hydra configuration, current provider/UUID/exclusive availability and release inputs. Write `execution-release-v1.json` with exact plan/source/cohort/ordered keys/authority/GPU7/limits and protected false. `python scripts/qd_ed_n28_supervise.py --plan <plan> --release <release> --status <N28>/execution/supervisor-status-v1.json`. Launcher creates execution directory before its lock. Old journals/proofs are untouched.
+
+All new valid cells need the original same-process generic audit plus profile-bound N28/native gate, even zero-guided. No supervisor CUDA re-audit. CPU receipt/hash/metrics checks retain legitimate missing metrics only when all guided/canonical denominators are zero. Missing cost stays explicit; no token zero imputation. Any new invalid/interrupted row closes remaining work. Status/journal disagreement preserves both prefixes and all observed costs and emits INVALID, never resume or promotion.
+
